  "_comment": "Verified-and-decoded store messages as the shared receivers hand them to this block (README section 3, \"Intake\"). Real Apple messages are signed JWS strings (`signedPayload`) and real Google messages are base64 Pub/Sub data; here they are decoded and reduced to the fields the block reads. All ids, tokens and the bundle/package name are placeholders. `delivery.event_id` is the Apple `notificationUUID` or the Google Pub/Sub `messageId`. Apple times are millisecond Unix times as in the store payloads; Google times are RFC 3339. `fetches` are reduced `purchases.subscriptionsv2.get` results that the block obtains after a Google message; `fetch_script` says which result each message sees and when the fetch started. Outcomes: applied, applied_no_change, stale, duplicate, unlinked, ignored. `apple_refund` and `apple_refund_reversed` are not routed to the handler: billing.virtual-currency records them and fires on_purchase_state_changed, and the chain refresh then sees these snapshots (sequence `apple_refund_then_reversal`).",
